          "text": "ELECTROENCEPHALOGRAM REPORT\n\nClinical Indication:\nEvaluation of episodic altered awareness.\n\nTechnique:\nRoutine EEG recorded using the international 10–20 electrode placement system. The study included wakefulness and drowsiness. Photic stimulation and hyperventilation were performed.\n\nFindings:\nThe waking background demonstrates a posterior dominant rhythm of 8 Hz that is symmetric and reactive to eye opening. Intermittent generalized theta slowing is present, with occasional brief runs of higher-amplitude delta activity. No focal slowing is identified.\n\nPhotic stimulation produces a symmetric driving response. Hyperventilation does not elicit additional abnormalities. No epileptiform discharges or electrographic seizures are recorded.\n\nImpression:\nAbnormal EEG due to intermittent generalized slowing, consistent with mild diffuse cerebral dysfunction. No epileptiform abnormalities or seizures are captured.",
